{
  "description": "Expected results for the search query syntax documented in CLAUDE.md. The web client runs this from src/lib/services/searchService.query.test.ts. Each client should run the same cases, so that a saved search means the same thing everywhere.",
  "rules": [
    "Matching ignores case. A plain word or *word* matches anywhere in the note's content or tags, including inside a longer word.",
    "word* and *word match the start and end of a word. Words are split on whitespace and punctuation.",
    "A quoted phrase matches those characters in that order. An unclosed quote runs to the end of the query.",
    "#tag matches any tag containing that text. Terms next to each other are ANDed.",
    "| joins the terms on either side into a group where any one may match, with or without spaces around it. A group can mix tags and text. Groups are ANDed with everything else.",
    "-word and -\"a phrase\" exclude notes whose content contains that text. -#tag excludes notes with a matching tag. An exclusion is always ANDed, and ends a | group.",
    "A lone -, # or * is an ordinary search for that character. A | with nothing on one side is ignored."
  ],
  "notes": [
